    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "PAN AMERICAN WORLD AIRWAYS\nAIR MAIL\n27 JULY 70.\nSPECIAL\nAIRMAIL\nVIA PAN - AM\nPAGO TO\nU. S. A.\nVIA AIR MAIL\nPAR AVION\nCORREO AEREO\nAIR MAIL\n727 JULY 70y\nSAMO\n20\nsene\nAIR MAIL\nSAMOA I SISIFO\nPAN AMERICAN AIRWAYS SAMOAN CLIPPER\nMr. H. G. Gulbransen\nRegional Vice President, Sales,\nPan American World Airways\nHONOLULU",
      "9259-0073B\n4\nSAN\nJUL\n3\n187U\n.M\n2014.061.011 a",
      "PAN AMERIC\nAN WORLD AIRWAYS\n21st July, 1970.\nMr H.G. Gulbransen,\nRegional Vice President, Sales,\nPan American World Airways,\nHONOLULU.\nDear Hack,\nFrom Samoa - greetings!\nPan Am has pleasure in sending you this first-flight cover\ncommemorating another milestone in aviation in the Pacific - the Western\nSamoa internal air service between Apia on Upolu and Assau on Savai 'i.\nNearly thirty-three years ago, Pan Am pioneered the air routes\nof the Pacific, linking New Zealand with the United States through Samoa.\nThough the flying-boats have been superseded by the jets -\nsoon by the 747 - Pan Am is honoured that Capt. Edwin C. Musick's \"Samoan\nClipper\" is included in the definitive airmail issue.\nIa soifua lava,\nbill\nW.L. ROLPH\nDirector-Sales, New Zealand\nAUCKLAND\nP.O. BOX 3919\n3 SHORTLAND STREET\nPan American World Airways Inc.\nAUCKLAND\nNEW ZEALAND\nIncorporated with Limited Liability in U.S.A."
    ],
